# Waqti Runtime — Layers 1–23 Generic Forward Checkpoint

## Implementation

Added one reusable `forward_layer(layer_index, hidden_state, position)` implementation in `transformer_layer.{h,cpp}`. Tensor names are resolved dynamically as `blk.<N>.*`; no layer-specific forward functions were created. The implementation reuses the verified mmap TensorView, RMSNorm, Q5_0/Q6_K/Q8_0 decoders, matvec, RoPE, GQA, single-token attention, concatenation, residual, SiLU, and SwiGLU operators.

The GGUF metadata scan found all required tensor families complete for Layers 0 through 23. Layer 0 was run through the generic path before executing the remaining layers and matched the saved Layer-0 second-residual checkpoint:

```text
layer0 first4 = -0.0849903, -0.3422503, 0.233653, -0.142844
layer0 output RMS = 0.340542
finite = true
```

## First divergence and repair

The first full run stopped at Layer 2 with:

```text
tensor type is not implemented by reference decoder
```

Metadata identified `blk.2.ffn_down.weight` as GGML type 12 (`Q4_K`). The existing Q4_K reference decoder was integrated into the common `tensor_decode` path. A direct type-12 decoder fixture was added and all tests passed before rerunning.

